    "## Evolution parameters and $\\rho_S(0)$\n",
    "\n",
    "Since **TENSO** is designed to handle realistic systems and structured environments, its default time units are typically expressed in femtoseconds (fs). Nevertheless, these units can be modified depending on the specifics of the simulation.\n",
    "\n",
    "- `end_time`: Final simulation time, specified in femtoseconds.\n",
    "- `dt`: Time step used for the integration of the dynamics.\n",
    "- `wfn`: Initial state of the system. In this case, the system starts in the ground state\n",
    "\n",
    "  $$\n",
    "  |\\Psi\\rangle = |0\\rangle.\n",
    "  $$\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "a59623f0",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "end_time = 40 #fs\n",
    "dt = 0.01\n",
    "wfn = np.array([0.0, 1.0], dtype=np.complex128)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3e94d6e2",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Time-dependent field\n",
    "\n",
    "Here, we illustrate the implementation of a Hadamard gate in a two-level system subject exclusively to pure dephasing. The objective is to coherently drive the system from the ground state to a superposition of the form\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "|\\Psi\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left( |0\\rangle + |1\\rangle \\right).\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "To achieve this, we employ the rotating wave approximation (RWA) and transform the Hamiltonian into the rotating frame defined by the laser frequency. The resulting Hamiltonian reads\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "H_{\\text{rot}} = \\frac{\\Delta\\epsilon - \\hbar\\omega_L}{2}\\,\\sigma_z + \\frac{\\mu E(t)}{2}\\,\\sigma_x,\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "where we define the detuning $\\delta = \\Delta\\epsilon - \\hbar\\omega_L$, which vanishes under resonant excitation. The laser pulse envelope, after these transformations, takes the form $E(t) = E_0 \\exp\\left(-\\frac{(t-t_0)^2}{2\\sigma^2}\\right)$. According to the area theorem, the required pulse amplitude is\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "E_0 = \\frac{\\pi \\hbar}{2\\mu\\sigma\\sqrt{2\\pi}}.\n",
    "$$\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 65,
   "id": "7a0e8a4b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "1.5707961147660308\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "cm_to_Ha = 1.23984e-4 / 27.211386    # cm^-1 to Hartree\n",
    "atomic_time_unit = 2.418884e-17      # 1 a.u. of time in seconds\n",
    "T_K = 100                            # Temperature in Kelvin\n",
    "kB_Ha = 3.166811563e-6               # Boltzmann constant in Hartree/K\n",
    "T_Ha = T_K * kB_Ha  \n",
    "FWHM_fs = 5#quantity(5, 'time')\n",
    "FWHM_fs2 = 5\n",
    "sigma_fs = quantity(FWHM_fs / 2.3548, 'time')\n",
    "sigma_fs2 = FWHM_fs2/ 2.3548\n",
    "sigma_au = sigma_fs2 * 1.0e-15 / atomic_time_unit  # Convertir fs a a.u.\n",
    "t0_au = quantity(10, 'time')#(6* 1e-15 / atomic_time_unit)#T_max_au / 2.0           \n",
    "t1_au = (20* 1.0e-15 / atomic_time_unit)               # Pulso centrado en la mitad\n",
    "t2_au = (35* 1.0e-15 / atomic_time_unit)               # Pulso centrado en la mitad\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# Se utiliza el momento dipolar de transiciÃ³n dado (en a.u.)\n",
    "mu = 3.31356454592 \n",
    "\n",
    "mu2 = 0.9823899964\n",
    "E0_pi = np.pi/2 / (mu * sigma_au * np.sqrt(2*np.pi))\n",
    "E0_pi2 = 2*np.pi / (mu2 * sigma_au * np.sqrt(2*np.pi))\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "muE = (mu * E0_pi)*219474.6313705 #cm-1\n",
    "muE = quantity(muE, 'energy')  \n",
    "\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "\n",
    "def semi(t):\n",
    "    # t, laser_center y sigma en fs (compatibles con quantity)\n",
    "    return  (muE/2) * np.exp(-0.5 * ((t - t0_au) / sigma_fs)**2)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(muE*np.sqrt(2*np.pi)*sigma_fs)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
